Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
As special arrangements need to be made (e.g. in most cases these items cannot be x-rayed) please ensure you provide the following information to our team once you have made your booking:
<ul>
	<li>Details of the Bone Marrow and/or Blood Products to be carried</li>
	<li>How these are to be carried, for example by dry shipper (esky type/mini vac)</li>
	<li>Provide a letter (on the hospitals or clinic’s letterhead) advising the contents of the dry shipper (esky/mini vac), dimensions and weight of the esky</li>
	<li>Whether dry ice is required</li>
	<li>The hospitals/clinics letter must confirm the fact that the contents are "non-dangerous/non-hazardous and non- infectious" and must be presented on check-in</li>
	<li>The flight details in which the courier is carrying the products</li>
</ul>
Qantas are only responsible for Qantas operated flights.<br />
<br />
Once you have obtained the above information, please contact our team and provide your Qantas booking reference so we may process your booking.<br />
<br />
If you require further assistance, please reply back to this email or contact the Qantas Customer Specific Needs team between 6am and 10pm (AEST), Monday to Sunday on 1800 177 474 (within Australia) or +61 2 9123 7471 (outside Australia) on1800 177 474, option 3.&nbsp;</body>
